Following are the 11 functions used in code in code-order:-

void gameload(int limit): 
	To load linked list structure according to difficulty of game.

void display(int limit):
	Displays the game layout which includes flag count and game board.

int subcountbomb(struct ground *g):
	Just a sub function for countbomb() to reduce code redundancy.

char countbomb(struct ground *g):
	Counts mines around the tile to be dug and returns value of number of mines around.
	This number is displayed in game board as a hint for players.

void digaround(struct ground *);

void subdigaround(struct ground *g):
	Just a sub function for digaround() to reduce code redundancy.
	Calls digaround(g)

void digaround(struct ground *g):
	Digs the tile which has no mine around that is g[row][col]->inground == ' '.
	Calls g[row][col]->inground = countbomb(g[row][col])
	If g[row][col]->inground == ' '
	Calls digaround(g[row][col])
	So it is a recursive function.
	It prevents game from getting boring as digging tiles without mines around one by one makes game boring and tedious to play.

void random(int limit,int totbomb,int row,int col):
	Sets bomb at random tiles by selecting random row col for linked list nodes with help of rand() and srand() functions.
	Also keeps the first dug tile (row, col) free of mines.
	By this function game gets a new board on every execution and every time when played again.

void validate(int *data):
	It validates int type data for any char type entry

void playgame(int limit):
	Decides totbomb on basis of limit.
	Controls while loop which ends (1)when all tiles except mines are dug or (2)any mine is dug.
	In case 1 you win and in case 2 you lose.
		Asks row and col for selected tile
		Also asks player to dig or flag and controls flag and dig count.
		When dig is selected it
			Calls random(limit,totbomb,row,col) for the first dig only.	
			Calls g[row][col]->inground = countbomb(g[row][col])
			g[row][col]->groundptr = &g[row][col]->inground
			If g[row][col]->inground == ' '
			Calls digaround(g[row][col])
			dig++
		When flag is selected
			If not flagged
			g[row][col]->onground=16
			flag--
			If already flagged then it is unflagged
			g[row][col]->onground='#'
			flag++

		Calls display(limit)

void emptymemory(int limit):
	It frees the memory each time game ends.
	So that memory is not wasted if players play game again and again without terminating program.
	Resets dig and flag to 0.

int main(): The driver function
	Gets limit (difficulty level).
	Calls gameload(limit)
	Calls playgame(limit)
	Calls emptymemory(limit)
	Controls loop for play again and exit.

